# A 3x2 grid of cells on paper, 64px pitch, each a 48x48 solid square cut by a mask.
# Top row, left to right:
# 1. Red square masked by `mask @m1`, a named invisible circle (radius 18): the square shows as a hard-edged red disc, the square's corners are gone.
# 2. Blue square masked by a noise field `mask simplex(10) > .5`: the square shows as a scatter of hard-edged blue blobs with paper gaps, no soft gradients.
# 3. Green square masked by a `mask` block holding two circles (radius 12, at the square's local offsets -10,-10 and 10,10: one upper left, one lower right): two separate green discs on paper, nothing between them.
# Bottom row, left to right:
# 4. Gold 56x56 square masked by `mask @m4` with `feather:5` on the draw: a gold disc that fades softly into paper with no hard rim: solid gold only near the center (r<=4), 84% strength at r 8, half strength at r 12 to 13, under 15% by r 18, and paper by r 25 (inside the square's 28px half-width).
# 5. A `layer` holding a red left half and a blue right half (two 24x48 rects), masked by `mask @m5` (a circle, radius 20): one disc split down the middle, red left and blue right, hard edge.
# 6. Gold 56x56 square clipped by `inside @m6` with `feather:5`: made by a clip instead of a mask, with the same fade as cell 4: solid only near the center (r<=4), half strength at r 12 to 13, paper by r 25.
@target structure/mask.png 192x128

circle 18 at:32,32 name:m1 fill:none
rect 48x48 at:32,32 fill:p.red
  mask @m1

rect 48x48 at:96,32 fill:p.blue name:speckle
  mask simplex(10) > .5

rect 48x48 at:160,32 fill:p.green
  mask
    circle 12 at:-10,-10
    circle 12 at:10,10

circle 14 at:32,96 name:m4 fill:none
rect 56x56 at:32,96 fill:p.gold feather:5
  mask @m4

circle 20 at:96,96 name:m5 fill:none
layer halves
  rect 24x48 at:84,96 fill:p.red
  rect 24x48 at:108,96 fill:p.blue
  mask @m5

circle 14 at:160,96 name:m6 fill:none
inside @m6 feather:5
  rect 56x56 at:160,96 fill:p.gold
